=B0C, you=E2=80=99re off by ~273.15 everywhere =E2=86=92 RMSE explodes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2526" data-end=3D"2688">
<p data-start=3D"2528" data-end=3D"2538"><strong data-start=3D"2528" data-e=
nd=3D"2536">Wind</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"2541" data-end=3D"2688">
<li data-start=3D"2541" data-end=3D"2605">
<p data-start=3D"2543" data-end=3D"2605">Variable might be <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"2561" data-end=3D"2568">m/s</strong>, but you use <strong data-start=
=3D"2582" data-end=3D"2590">km/h</strong> or vice-versa.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2608" data-end=3D"2688">
<p data-start=3D"2610" data-end=3D"2688">Or they want <strong data-start=3D=
"2623" data-end=3D"2641">u/v components</strong>, and you give <strong data=
-start=3D"2656" data-end=3D"2670">speed only</strong> (or wrong order).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2690" data-end=3D"2768">
<p data-start=3D"2692" data-end=3D"2711"><strong data-start=3D"2692" data-e=
nd=3D"2709">Precipitation</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"2714" data-end=3D"2768">
<li data-start=3D"2714" data-end=3D"2768">
<p data-start=3D"2716" data-end=3D"2768">mm vs m vs kg/m=C2=B2 =E2=80=93 ea=
sy to be off by factor 10=E2=80=931000.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2770" data-end=3D"2844">=F0=9F=91=89 <strong data-start=3D=
