<p data-start=3D"2994" data-end=3D"3095">If you=E2=80=99re proxying another=
 API (e.g., Open-Meteo) check that you don=E2=80=99t double-convert or mis-=
convert.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3097" data-end=3D"3100">
<h3 data-start=3D"3102" data-end=3D"3144">(B) <strong data-start=3D"3110" d=
ata-end=3D"3144">Wrong time / horizon alignment</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3146" data-end=3D"3162">Another classic:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3164" data-end=3D"3309">
<li data-start=3D"3164" data-end=3D"3191">
<p data-start=3D"3166" data-end=3D"3191">Task: =E2=80=9CForecast at T+48h=
=E2=80=9D</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3192" data-end=3D"3309">
<p data-start=3D"3194" data-end=3D"3224">Your model: gives snapshot at:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3227" data-end=3D"3309">
<li data-start=3D"3227" data-end=3D"3251">
<p data-start=3D"3229" data-end=3D"3251">T (current time), or</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3254" data-end=3D"3266">
<p data-start=3D"3256" data-end=3D"3266">T+24, or</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3269" data-end=3D"3309">
<p data-start=3D"3271" data-end=3D"3309">Nearest grid time rounded incorrec=
tly.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3311" data-end=3D"3405">Even if your model is good, <stron=
g data-start=3D"3339" data-end=3D"3379">being off by 1=E2=80=932 days in fo=
recasting</strong> is catastrophic for RMSE.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3407" data-end=3D"3423">Things to check:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3425" data-end=3D"3677">
<li data-start=3D"3425" data-end=3D"3498">
<p data-start=3D"3427" data-end=3D"3498">Are you using <strong data-start=
=3D"3441" data-end=3D"3448">UTC</strong> everywhere? (ERA5 and most baselin=
es are in UTC.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3499" data-end=3D"3572">
<p data-start=3D"3501" data-end=3D"3572">Are you reading the <strong data-s=
tart=3D"3521" data-end=3D"3544">lead time / horizon</strong> from the reque=
st correctly?</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3573" data-end=3D"3677">
<p data-start=3D"3575" data-end=3D"3677">If you use an API (Open-Meteo, etc=
.), are you asking for the same <strong data-start=3D"3641" data-end=3D"365=
8">forecast time</strong> that Zeus expects?</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3679" data-end=3D"3682">
<h3 data-start=3D"3684" data-end=3D"3717">(C) <strong data-start=3D"3692" d=
ata-end=3D"3717">Shape / indexing bugs</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3719" data-end=3D"3770">Even simple indexing mistakes can =
produce nonsense:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3772" data-end=3D"3995">
<li data-start=3D"3772" data-end=3D"3805">
<p data-start=3D"3774" data-end=3D"3805">Swapped <strong data-start=3D"3782=
" data-end=3D"3804">latitude/longitude</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3806" data-end=3D"3858">
<p data-start=3D"3808" data-end=3D"3858">Swapped <strong data-start=3D"3816=
" data-end=3D"3835">batch dimension</strong> vs <strong data-start=3D"3839"=
 data-end=3D"3857">time dimension</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3859" data-end=3D"3936">
<p data-start=3D"3861" data-end=3D"3936">Returning values for <strong data-=
start=3D"3882" data-end=3D"3910">the wrong variable index</strong> inside t=
he output tensor.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3937" data-end=3D"3995">
<p data-start=3D"3939" data-end=3D"3995">Filling the wrong slice (e.g., dew=
point vs temperature).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3997" data-end=3D"4164">If you=E2=80=99re using the refere=
nce <code data-start=3D"4027" data-end=3D"4042">run_neuron.py</code> and mo=
difying it, or customizing a <code data-start=3D"4078" data-end=3D"4085">Mi=
ner</code> class in <code data-start=3D"4095" data-end=3D"4105">neurons/</c=
ode>, it=E2=80=99s easy to get one array misaligned and hurt all tasks.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4166" data-end=3D"4181">=F0=9F=91=89 What I=E2=80=99d do:<=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"4183" data-end=3D"4454">
<li data-start=3D"4183" data-end=3D"4326">
<p data-start=3D"4185" data-end=3D"4238">Add <strong data-start=3D"4189" da=
ta-end=3D"4200">asserts</strong> in your miner right before returning:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4241" data-end=3D"4326">
<li data-start=3D"4241" data-end=3D"4268">
<p data-start=3D"4243" data-end=3D"4268">Shape is exactly as spec.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4271" data-end=3D"4291">
<p data-start=3D"4273" data-end=3D"4291">No <code data-start=3D"4276" data-=
end=3D"4281">NaN</code> or <code data-start=3D"4285" data-end=3D"4290">inf<=
/code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4294" data-end=3D"4326">
<p data-start=3D"4296" data-end=3D"4326">Lat/lon are in allowed ranges.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4327" data-end=3D"4454">
<p data-start=3D"4329" data-end=3D"4345">Temporarily log:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4348" data-end=3D"4454">
<li data-start=3D"4348" data-end=3D"4380">
<p data-start=3D"4350" data-end=3D"4380">First few outputs per request.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4383" data-end=3D"4454">
<p data-start=3D"4385" data-end=3D"4454">The corresponding input metadata (=
time, lat, lon, horizon, variable).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4456" data-end=3D"4459">
<h3 data-start=3D"4461" data-end=3D"4511">(D) <strong data-start=3D"4469" d=
ata-end=3D"4511">Penalties from late / broken responses</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4513" data-end=3D"4667">From the Gaia/Zeus back-and-forth,=
 we know: <strong data-start=3D"4557" data-end=3D"4572">RMSE =3D -1.0</stro=
ng> is a <em data-start=3D"4578" data-end=3D"4594">penalty marker</em> used=
 for late/invalid responses. <span class=3D"" data-state=3D"closed"><span c=
lass=3D"ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] a=
nimate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid=3D"webpage-citation-pill"><a href=
