=E2=80=93 Something lightweight<br data-start=3D"585" data-end=3D"588">
=E2=80=93 Or even external API-based predictions (slow but workable)</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"650" data-end=3D"685">=E2=9C=94 No GPU needed for inferen=
ce</h3>
<p data-start=3D"686" data-end=3D"771">They explicitly say:<br data-start=
=3D"706" data-end=3D"709">
<strong data-start=3D"709" data-end=3D"771">=E2=80=9CGPU is not required fo=
r inference while running a miner.=E2=80=9D</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"773" data-end=3D"784">That means:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"786" data-end=3D"881">
<li data-start=3D"786" data-end=3D"820">
<p data-start=3D"788" data-end=3D"820">You don=E2=80=99t need a GPU to <em =
data-start=3D"812" data-end=3D"818">mine</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"821" data-end=3D"860">
<p data-start=3D"823" data-end=3D"860">You don=E2=80=99t need to train huge=
 models</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"861" data-end=3D"881">
<p data-start=3D"863" data-end=3D"881">You can run on CPU</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"883" data-end=3D"921"><strong data-start=3D"883" data-end=
=3D"921">This is how 90% of miners operate.</strong></p>
<hr data-start=3D"923" data-end=3D"926">
<h1 data-start=3D"928" data-end=3D"968"><strong data-start=3D"930" data-end=
=3D"966">2. Researchers (advanced miners)</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"969" data-end=3D"1012">These are the people who use the su=
bnet to:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1014" data-end=3D"1176">
<li data-start=3D"1014" data-end=3D"1045">
<p data-start=3D"1016" data-end=3D"1045">Train larger weather models</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1046" data-end=3D"1081">
<p data-start=3D"1048" data-end=3D"1081">Use NVIDIA A100 / H100 clusters</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1082" data-end=3D"1112">
<p data-start=3D"1084" data-end=3D"1112">Produce stronger forecasts</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1113" data-end=3D"1139">
<p data-start=3D"1115" data-end=3D"1139">Upload trained weights</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1140" data-end=3D"1176">
<p data-start=3D"1142" data-end=3D"1176">Compete for top performance scores=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1178" data-end=3D"1250">Zeus encourages this because it in=
creases the subnet=E2=80=99s scientific value.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1252" data-end=3D"1392">These =E2=80=9Cresearch miners=E2=
=80=9D actually <strong data-start=3D"1285" data-end=3D"1346">train GraphCa=
st-like, FourCastNet-like, Pangu-like models</strong>.<br data-start=3D"134=
7" data-end=3D"1350">
But training those requires <strong data-start=3D"1378" data-end=3D"1391">G=
PU power</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1394" data-end=3D"1420">That's why the guide says:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"1422" data-end=3D"1488">
<p data-start=3D"1424" data-end=3D"1488">=E2=80=9CA GPU is required for tra=
ining=E2=80=A6 unless you want to wait weeks=E2=80=A6=E2=80=9D</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"1490" data-end=3D"1560">This is only referring to the <str=
ong data-start=3D"1520" data-end=3D"1537">training side</strong>, not infer=
ence/mining.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1562" data-end=3D"1605"><strong data-start=3D"1562" data-e=
nd=3D"1604">You are NOT required to train anything</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1607" data-end=3D"1610">
<h1 data-start=3D"1612" data-end=3D"1649">=F0=9F=94=A5 So why is this menti=
oned at all?</h1>
<p data-start=3D"1651" data-end=3D"1706">Because Zeus wants two things happ=
ening simultaneously:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1708" data-end=3D"1764"><strong data-start=3D"1712" data-=
end=3D"1762">(A) Miners providing predictions =E2=86=92 earning TAO</strong=
></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1765" data-end=3D"1786">These miners can run:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1788" data-end=3D"1860">
<li data-start=3D"1788" data-end=3D"1799">
<p data-start=3D"1790" data-end=3D"1799">Simple ML</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1800" data-end=3D"1811">
<p data-start=3D"1802" data-end=3D"1811">Medium ML</p>
