<p data-start=3D"359" data-end=3D"423">You train a model that predicts <str=
ong data-start=3D"391" data-end=3D"408">only dewpoint</strong>, nothing els=
e.</p>
<p data-start=3D"425" data-end=3D"450">If you want to train for:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"452" data-end=3D"629">
<li data-start=3D"452" data-end=3D"470">
<p data-start=3D"454" data-end=3D"470"><code data-start=3D"454" data-end=3D=
"470">2m_temperature</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"471" data-end=3D"498">
<p data-start=3D"473" data-end=3D"498"><code data-start=3D"473" data-end=3D=
"498">10m_u_component_of_wind</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"499" data-end=3D"526">
<p data-start=3D"501" data-end=3D"526"><code data-start=3D"501" data-end=3D=
"526">10m_v_component_of_wind</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"555">
<p data-start=3D"529" data-end=3D"555"><code data-start=3D"529" data-end=3D=
"555">100m_u_component_of_wind</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"556" data-end=3D"584">
<p data-start=3D"558" data-end=3D"584"><code data-start=3D"558" data-end=3D=
"584">100m_v_component_of_wind</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"585" data-end=3D"605">
<p data-start=3D"587" data-end=3D"605"><code data-start=3D"587" data-end=3D=
"605">surface_pressure</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"606" data-end=3D"629">
<p data-start=3D"608" data-end=3D"629"><code data-start=3D"608" data-end=3D=
"629">total_precipitation</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"631" data-end=3D"692">=E2=80=A6then you run the training s=
cript <strong data-start=3D"665" data-end=3D"691">once for each variable</s=
trong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"694" data-end=3D"825">This is normal because <strong data-=
start=3D"717" data-end=3D"766">Zeus validator sends one variable per reques=
t</strong>, and your miner currently predicts one variable at a time.</p>
