]">+1</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
<p data-start=3D"262" data-end=3D"335">Here=E2=80=99s what that means for y=
our training, along with some considerations.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"337" data-end=3D"340">
<h2 data-start=3D"342" data-end=3D"370">=E2=9C=85 What this means for you</=
h2>
<ul data-start=3D"372" data-end=3D"617">
<li data-start=3D"372" data-end=3D"443">
<p data-start=3D"374" data-end=3D"443">You <em data-start=3D"378" data-end=
=3D"383">can</em> download ERA5 from <strong data-start=3D"403" data-end=3D=
"427">January 1940 onwards</strong>, if you want.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"444" data-end=3D"522">
<p data-start=3D"446" data-end=3D"522">More data =3D potentially better tra=
ining (more diverse climate conditions).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"523" data-end=3D"617">
<p data-start=3D"525" data-end=3D"617">If you have storage and compute capa=
city, using older data can help your model generalize.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"619" data-end=3D"622">
<h2 data-start=3D"624" data-end=3D"672">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Some caveats and=
 practical recommendations</h2>
<p data-start=3D"674" data-end=3D"796">Even though ERA5 goes back to 1940, =
you may want to <strong data-start=3D"726" data-end=3D"743">choose wisely</=
strong> how much of that span you actually use for training:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"798" data-end=3D"840">1. <strong data-start=3D"805" data-=
end=3D"838">Quality / Observation Density</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"841" data-end=3D"1015">
<li data-start=3D"841" data-end=3D"942">
<p data-start=3D"843" data-end=3D"942">Earlier years (1940=E2=80=931950s) h=
ave <strong data-start=3D"875" data-end=3D"897">fewer observations</strong>=
, so the reanalysis has higher uncertainty.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"943" data-end=3D"1015">
<p data-start=3D"945" data-end=3D"1015">Model performance may be worse for =
older data; it may introduce noise.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1017" data-end=3D"1056">2. <strong data-start=3D"1024" da=
ta-end=3D"1054">Computation / Storage Cost</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1057" data-end=3D"1255">
<li data-start=3D"1057" data-end=3D"1114">
<p data-start=3D"1059" data-end=3D"1114">Using decades of hourly data is <s=
trong data-start=3D"1091" data-end=3D"1099">huge</strong> =E2=80=94 terabyt=
es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1115" data-end=3D"1255">
<p data-start=3D"1117" data-end=3D"1255">For training a practical model, yo=
u might pick a subset (e.g., last 5=E2=80=9310 years) and maybe use older y=
ears for augmentation or fine-tuning.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1257" data-end=3D"1292">3. <strong data-start=3D"1264" da=
ta-end=3D"1290">Climate Change / Shift</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1293" data-end=3D"1561">
<li data-start=3D"1293" data-end=3D"1351">
<p data-start=3D"1295" data-end=3D"1351">Weather patterns change over decad=
es (climate trends).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1483">
<p data-start=3D"1354" data-end=3D"1483">If you include too old data, you m=
ight have to handle <strong data-start=3D"1408" data-end=3D"1428">non-stati=
onarity</strong> in training (the model sees very different regimes).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1484" data-end=3D"1561">
<p data-start=3D"1486" data-end=3D"1561">Sometimes training on recent data =
gives better forecasting for recent asks.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1563" data-end=3D"1610">4. <strong data-start=3D"1570" da=
ta-end=3D"1608">Align with Zeus Variables / Format</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1611" data-end=3D"1861">
<li data-start=3D"1611" data-end=3D"1708">
<p data-start=3D"1613" data-end=3D"1708">Make sure your downloaded data <em=
 data-start=3D"1644" data-end=3D"1654">includes</em> the variables you need=
 (as in our training script).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1709" data-end=3D"1861">
<p data-start=3D"1711" data-end=3D"1861">And your resolution and grid match=
 what your miner expects (0.25=C2=B0 grid, etc.). The dataset page confirms=
 this. <span class=3D"" data-state=3D"closed"><span class=3D"ms-1 inline-fl=
ex max-w-full items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_eas=
e-in]" data-testid=3D"webpage-citation-pill"><a href=3D"https://earthdatahu=
