></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1863" data-end=3D"1866">
<h2 data-start=3D"1868" data-end=3D"1899">=F0=9F=8E=AF My recommendation fo=
r you</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1901" data-end=3D"2020">Since your goal is to improve your=
 miner (and you currently have performance of -36%), I suggest this initial=
 strategy:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2022" data-end=3D"2463">
<li data-start=3D"2022" data-end=3D"2128">
<p data-start=3D"2024" data-end=3D"2128">Download <strong data-start=3D"203=
3" data-end=3D"2053">recent 1-2 years</strong> of data (for example 2023, 2=
024) to keep things manageable and relevant.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2129" data-end=3D"2163">
<p data-start=3D"2131" data-end=3D"2163">Then train your model on that.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2164" data-end=3D"2310">
<p data-start=3D"2166" data-end=3D"2310">After your model works and baselin=
e improves to positive territory, you can <strong data-start=3D"2242" data-=
end=3D"2252">expand</strong> to older years (say 2015-2024) to boost genera=
lization.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2311" data-end=3D"2463">
<p data-start=3D"2313" data-end=3D"2463">Only later if you want to push for=
 top performance (and have storage/compute), include older decades (e.g., 1=
940-2015) and consider domain adaptation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2465" data-end=3D"2468">
<p data-start=3D"2470" data-end=3D"2643">If you like, I can <em data-start=
