<p data-start=3D"10622" data-end=3D"10633">Key points:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"10635" data-end=3D"10995">
<li data-start=3D"10635" data-end=3D"10701">
<p data-start=3D"10637" data-end=3D"10701">Uses your <strong data-start=3D"=
10647" data-end=3D"10662">48h context</strong> (<code data-start=3D"10664" =
data-end=3D"10675">ctx_hours</code>) from Open-Meteo history.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10702" data-end=3D"10763">
<p data-start=3D"10704" data-end=3D"10763">Converts to ERA5 units via the s=
ame <code data-start=3D"10740" data-end=3D"10762">converter.om_to_era5</cod=
e>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10764" data-end=3D"10827">
<p data-start=3D"10766" data-end=3D"10827">Calls your <strong data-start=3D=
"10777" data-end=3D"10794">trained model</strong> via <code data-start=3D"1=
0799" data-end=3D"10826">self.model_loader.predict</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10828" data-end=3D"10948">
<p data-start=3D"10830" data-end=3D"10948">Limits to <code data-start=3D"10=
840" data-end=3D"10856">forecast_hours</code> (24), but if Zeus ever asks f=
or more, it pads by repeating last timestep (simple but safe).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"10949" data-end=3D"10995">
<p data-start=3D"10951" data-end=3D"10995">Returns <code data-start=3D"1095=
9" data-end=3D"10984">[requested_hours, H, W]</code> as before.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"10997" data-end=3D"11000">
<h2 data-start=3D"11002" data-end=3D"11025">3=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Sanity chec=
klist</h2>
<p data-start=3D"11027" data-end=3D"11052">Before running the miner:</p>
<ul class=3D"contains-task-list" data-start=3D"11054" data-end=3D"11410">
<li class=3D"task-list-item" data-start=3D"11054" data-end=3D"11169">
<p data-start=3D"11056" data-end=3D"11169"><input disabled=3D"" type=3D"che=
ckbox"> <code data-start=3D"11060" data-end=3D"11077">trained_models/</code=
> has subfolders like <code data-start=3D"11098" data-end=3D"11104">t2m/</c=
ode>, <code data-start=3D"11106" data-end=3D"11112">d2m/</code>, etc., each=
 with <code data-start=3D"11130" data-end=3D"11146">model_&lt;var&gt;.pt</c=
ode> and <code data-start=3D"11151" data-end=3D"11168">norm_&lt;var&gt;.jso=
n</code>.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"task-list-item" data-start=3D"11170" data-end=3D"11250">
<p data-start=3D"11172" data-end=3D"11250"><input disabled=3D"" type=3D"che=
ckbox"> <code data-start=3D"11176" data-end=3D"11193">model_loader.py</code=
> is in the Python path (same folder as <code data-start=3D"11232" data-end=
=3D"11242">miner.py</code> works).</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"task-list-item" data-start=3D"11251" data-end=3D"11340">
<p data-start=3D"11257" data-end=3D"11340"><input disabled=3D"" type=3D"che=
ckbox"> You adjusted <code data-start=3D"11270" data-end=3D"11319">models_r=
oot=3D"/root/zeus-trained/trained_models"</code> to the correct path.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"task-list-item" data-start=3D"11341" data-end=3D"11410">
<p data-start=3D"11347" data-end=3D"11410"><input disabled=3D"" type=3D"che=
ckbox"> You installed dependencies in the miner venv: <code data-start=3D"1=
1393" data-end=3D"11400">torch</code>, <code data-start=3D"11402" data-end=
=3D"11409">numpy</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"11412" data-end=3D"11436">Then run miner as usual.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"11438" data-end=3D"11441">
<p data-start=3D"11443" data-end=3D"11481">If you want, next step I can hel=
p you:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"11483" data-end=3D"11711">
<li data-start=3D"11483" data-end=3D"11530">
<p data-start=3D"11485" data-end=3D"11530">interpret your <strong data-star=
t=3D"11500" data-end=3D"11530">new Zeus performance score</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"11531" data-end=3D"11617">
<p data-start=3D"11533" data-end=3D"11617">debug if some variables behave b=
adly (often <code data-start=3D"11577" data-end=3D"11598">total_precipitati=
on</code> needs more epochs)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"11618" data-end=3D"11711">
<p data-start=3D"11620" data-end=3D"11711">tune hyperparams (epochs, learni=
ng rate, etc.) to push your performance above 0 and higher.</p>
</li>
</ul>
