<p data-start=3D"531" data-end=3D"543">This script:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"545" data-end=3D"742">
<li data-start=3D"545" data-end=3D"583">
<p data-start=3D"547" data-end=3D"583">Downloads each variable (if missing)=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"584" data-end=3D"624">
<p data-start=3D"586" data-end=3D"624">Trains each variable one-by-one on G=
PU</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"625" data-end=3D"695">
<p data-start=3D"627" data-end=3D"695">Saves all <code data-start=3D"637" d=
ata-end=3D"642">.pt</code> and <code data-start=3D"647" data-end=3D"660">no=
rm_*.json</code> files into <code data-start=3D"672" data-end=3D"695">train=
ed_models/&lt;var&gt;/</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"696" data-end=3D"742">
<p data-start=3D"698" data-end=3D"742">Supports retries, logging, epochs li=
st, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"744" data-end=3D"902">=F0=9F=91=89 This handles <strong da=
ta-start=3D"760" data-end=3D"779">Automation only</strong><br data-start=3D=
"779" data-end=3D"782">
=F0=9F=91=89 It does NOT change the model architecture<br data-start=3D"826=
" data-end=3D"829">
=F0=9F=91=89 It does NOT load models into miner<br data-start=3D"866" data-=
end=3D"869">
=F0=9F=91=89 It is only about training jobs</p>
<hr data-start=3D"904" data-end=3D"907">
<h1 data-start=3D"909" data-end=3D"972">=F0=9F=9F=A9 <strong data-start=3D"=
914" data-end=3D"970">2) Improved UNet architecture for higher Zeus scores<=
/strong></h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"973" data-end=3D"1017">=F0=9F=92=A1 Purpose: Increase for=
ecast accuracy</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1018" data-end=3D"1068">This is a <strong data-start=3D"10=
28" data-end=3D"1053">better neural network</strong>, not a script.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1070" data-end=3D"1082">For example:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1084" data-end=3D"1334">
<li data-start=3D"1084" data-end=3D"1099">
<p data-start=3D"1086" data-end=3D"1099">Deeper UNet</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1100" data-end=3D"1119">
<p data-start=3D"1102" data-end=3D"1119">Residual blocks</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1120" data-end=3D"1153">
<p data-start=3D"1122" data-end=3D"1153">UNet++ dense skip connections</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1154" data-end=3D"1174">
<p data-start=3D"1156" data-end=3D"1174">Attention blocks</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1175" data-end=3D"1193">
<p data-start=3D"1177" data-end=3D"1193">Better padding</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1194" data-end=3D"1218">
<p data-start=3D"1196" data-end=3D"1218">Normalization layers</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1219" data-end=3D"1277">
<p data-start=3D"1221" data-end=3D"1277">Smaller dilation receptive field f=
or local forecasting</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1278" data-end=3D"1334">
<p data-start=3D"1280" data-end=3D"1334">Better multi-scale structure (Zeus=
 grids vary in size)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1336" data-end=3D"1350">This improves:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1492">
<li data-start=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1360">
<p data-start=3D"1354" data-end=3D"1360">RMSE</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1361" data-end=3D"1382">
<p data-start=3D"1363" data-end=3D"1382">spatial coherence</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1383" data-end=3D"1396">
<p data-start=3D"1385" data-end=3D"1396">stability</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1397" data-end=3D"1429">
<p data-start=3D"1399" data-end=3D"1429">performance on all variables</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1430" data-end=3D"1492">
<p data-start=3D"1432" data-end=3D"1492">EXCEPT <code data-start=3D"1439" d=
ata-end=3D"1460">total_precipitation</code> (which still needs many epochs)=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1494" data-end=3D"1612">=F0=9F=91=89 This changes <strong =
data-start=3D"1510" data-end=3D"1527">model quality</strong><br data-start=
=3D"1527" data-end=3D"1530">
=F0=9F=91=89 It affects <strong data-start=3D"1544" data-end=3D"1564">train=
ing results</strong><br data-start=3D"1564" data-end=3D"1567">
=F0=9F=91=89 It requires <strong data-start=3D"1582" data-end=3D"1610">modi=
fying train_model.py</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"1614" data-end=3D"1694">It is <strong data-start=3D"1620" =
data-end=3D"1635">independent</strong> from the training scheduler, loader,=
 or file organization.</p>
