<p data-start=3D"156" data-end=3D"202">The Copernicus CDS API <strong data-=
start=3D"179" data-end=3D"192">throttles</strong> based on:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"204" data-end=3D"290">
<li data-start=3D"204" data-end=3D"225">
<p data-start=3D"206" data-end=3D"225">requests per minute</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"226" data-end=3D"250">
<p data-start=3D"228" data-end=3D"250">concurrent connections</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"251" data-end=3D"290">
<p data-start=3D"253" data-end=3D"290">user CPU quota in their backend queu=
e</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"292" data-end=3D"307">So we must add:</p>
<h1 data-start=3D"309" data-end=3D"353">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"313=
" data-end=3D"353">Backoff + Staggering Between Workers</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"355" data-end=3D"380">We=E2=80=99ll fix it in 3 layers:</p=
>
<hr data-start=3D"382" data-end=3D"385">
<h1 data-start=3D"387" data-end=3D"427">=F0=9F=9F=A9 1. <strong data-start=
=3D"395" data-end=3D"425">Stagger worker start times</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"428" data-end=3D"511">Without this, all workers start at t=
he exact same millisecond =E2=86=92 instant rate-limit.</p>
<p data-start=3D"513" data-end=3D"567">We add a small random sleep before e=
ach worker starts:</p>
