ple terms.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"207" data-end=3D"210">
<h2 data-start=3D"212" data-end=3D"258">1=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 How much data d=
o you actually have now?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"260" data-end=3D"287">With your current settings:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"289" data-end=3D"551">
<li data-start=3D"289" data-end=3D"348">
<p data-start=3D"291" data-end=3D"348"><strong data-start=3D"291" data-end=
=3D"300">Grid:</strong> 1=C2=B0 =E2=86=92 about <strong data-start=3D"312" =
data-end=3D"346">181 =C3=97 360 =E2=89=88 65,000 grid points</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"349" data-end=3D"409">
<p data-start=3D"351" data-end=3D"409"><strong data-start=3D"351" data-end=
=3D"371">Time resolution:</strong> every <strong data-start=3D"378" data-en=
d=3D"389">3 hours</strong> =E2=86=92 8 steps per day</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"410" data-end=3D"448">
<p data-start=3D"412" data-end=3D"448"><strong data-start=3D"412" data-end=
=3D"426">One month:</strong> ~30 MB per variable</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"449" data-end=3D"498">
<p data-start=3D"451" data-end=3D"498"><strong data-start=3D"451" data-end=
=3D"475">One year (12=C3=9730 MB):</strong> ~360 MB per variable</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"499" data-end=3D"551">
<p data-start=3D"501" data-end=3D"551"><strong data-start=3D"501" data-end=
=3D"528">Four years (2022=E2=80=932025):</strong> ~1.4 GB per variable</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"553" data-end=3D"589">That=E2=80=99s <strong data-start=3D=
"560" data-end=3D"569">a LOT</strong> of training signal:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"591" data-end=3D"735">
<li data-start=3D"591" data-end=3D"634">
<p data-start=3D"593" data-end=3D"634">Time steps per year: 8 =C3=97 365 =
=E2=89=88 <strong data-start=3D"624" data-end=3D"632">2920</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"635" data-end=3D"697">
<p data-start=3D"637" data-end=3D"697">Sliding windows for context/forecast=
: thousands of samples</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"698" data-end=3D"735">
<p data-start=3D"700" data-end=3D"735">Each sample has ~65k spatial points<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"737" data-end=3D"814">You absolutely do <strong data-start=
=3D"755" data-end=3D"762">not</strong> need terabytes of data to train a so=
lid Zeus model.</p>
