</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start=3D"2055" data-end=3D"2137">The model doesn=E2=80=99t care if =
those steps are 1h or 3h apart =E2=80=94 it just sees sequences.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2139" data-end=3D"2267">We can adjust your <code data-star=
t=3D"2158" data-end=3D"2174">train_model.py</code> and miner integration la=
ter to make this <strong data-start=3D"2216" data-end=3D"2238">exactly cons=
istent</strong> with Zeus=E2=80=99s 48-hour horizon.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2269" data-end=3D"2272">
<h2 data-start=3D"2274" data-end=3D"2323">4=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Will Zeus val=
idators be unhappy with this?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2325" data-end=3D"2332">No =F0=9F=99=82</p>
<p data-start=3D"2334" data-end=3D"2349">Zeus only sees:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2351" data-end=3D"2462">
<li data-start=3D"2351" data-end=3D"2389">
<p data-start=3D"2353" data-end=3D"2389">Your <strong data-start=3D"2358" d=
ata-end=3D"2373">predictions</strong> at their grid</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2390" data-end=3D"2431">
<p data-start=3D"2392" data-end=3D"2431">Not your original training resolut=
ion</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2432" data-end=3D"2462">
<p data-start=3D"2434" data-end=3D"2462">Not your ERA5 grid details</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2464" data-end=3D"2475">As long as:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2477" data-end=3D"2616">
<li data-start=3D"2477" data-end=3D"2540">
<p data-start=3D"2479" data-end=3D"2540">Your model predicts <strong data-s=
tart=3D"2499" data-end=3D"2538">correct temperatures / winds / etc.</strong=
></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2541" data-end=3D"2580">
<p data-start=3D"2543" data-end=3D"2580">You handle time alignment correctl=
y</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2581" data-end=3D"2616">
<p data-start=3D"2583" data-end=3D"2616">Your inference is stable + fast</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2618" data-end=3D"2631">=E2=80=A6you=E2=80=99re good.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2633" data-end=3D"2714">If later you want to push from, sa=
y, <strong data-start=3D"2670" data-end=3D"2691">+10% =E2=86=92 +25% score<=
/strong>, then we can consider:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2716" data-end=3D"2804">
<li data-start=3D"2716" data-end=3D"2740">
<p data-start=3D"2718" data-end=3D"2740">Going from 1=C2=B0 =E2=86=92 0.5=
=C2=B0</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2741" data-end=3D"2804">
<p data-start=3D"2743" data-end=3D"2804">Or 3h =E2=86=92 1h for specific tr=
icky variables (like precipitation)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2806" data-end=3D"2875">But for <strong data-start=3D"2814=
" data-end=3D"2836">first strong miner</strong>, 1=C2=B0 + 3h is a smart, p=
ractical choice.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2877" data-end=3D"2880">
<h2 data-start=3D"2882" data-end=3D"2890">TL;DR</h2>
<blockquote data-start=3D"2892" data-end=3D"3034">
<p data-start=3D"2894" data-end=3D"3034">=F0=9F=92=AC <strong data-start=3D=
"2897" data-end=3D"2941">=E2=80=9CIs 30 MB per file enough for training?=E2=
=80=9D</strong><br data-start=3D"2941" data-end=3D"2944">
=F0=9F=91=89 <strong data-start=3D"2947" data-end=3D"3034">Yes. It=E2=80=99=
s more than enough for a strong Zeus model, especially for a first version.=
</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"3036" data-end=3D"3045">You have:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3047" data-end=3D"3160">
<li data-start=3D"3047" data-end=3D"3071">
<p data-start=3D"3049" data-end=3D"3071">Plenty of time steps</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3072" data-end=3D"3102">
<p data-start=3D"3074" data-end=3D"3102">Plenty of spatial coverage</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3103" data-end=3D"3128">
<p data-start=3D"3105" data-end=3D"3128">Much faster downloads</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3129" data-end=3D"3160">
<p data-start=3D"3131" data-end=3D"3160">Much easier training on GPU</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3162" data-end=3D"3165">
<p data-start=3D"3167" data-end=3D"3194">If you=E2=80=99d like, next we can=
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3196" data-end=3D"3457">
<li data-start=3D"3196" data-end=3D"3275">
<p data-start=3D"3198" data-end=3D"3275">Adjust <code data-start=3D"3205" d=
ata-end=3D"3221">train_model.py</code> to use <strong data-start=3D"3229" d=
ata-end=3D"3257">16 context / 16 forecast</strong> for 3-hour data</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3276" data-end=3D"3342">
<p data-start=3D"3278" data-end=3D"3342">Generate the <strong data-start=3D=
"3291" data-end=3D"3317">train_all_variables.sh</strong> for 2022=E2=80=932=
025, 1=C2=B0 + 3h</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3343" data-end=3D"3457">
<p data-start=3D"3345" data-end=3D"3457">Then finalize the <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"3363" data-end=3D"3399">model loader + miner integration</strong> so =
your miner actually starts using these trained models.</p>
</li>
</ul>
