<p data-start=3D"5972" data-end=3D"6021"><strong data-start=3D"5972" data-e=
nd=3D"5991">Better capacity</strong> =E2=86=92 lower loss, especially for:<=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"6024" data-end=3D"6096">
<li data-start=3D"6024" data-end=3D"6047">
<p data-start=3D"6026" data-end=3D"6047">total_precipitation</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6050" data-end=3D"6059">
<p data-start=3D"6052" data-end=3D"6059">winds</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6062" data-end=3D"6096">
<p data-start=3D"6064" data-end=3D"6096">tricky coastal/terrain regions</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6097" data-end=3D"6250">
<p data-start=3D"6099" data-end=3D"6176">Handles <strong data-start=3D"6107=
" data-end=3D"6136">0.5=C2=B0 grids and odd shapes</strong> (361=C3=97720, =
359=C3=97719, etc.)<br data-start=3D"6161" data-end=3D"6164">
thanks to:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6179" data-end=3D"6250">
<li data-start=3D"6179" data-end=3D"6212">
<p data-start=3D"6181" data-end=3D"6212">safe cropping in each UpBlock</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6215" data-end=3D"6250">
<p data-start=3D"6217" data-end=3D"6250">final cropping to <code data-start=
=3D"6235" data-end=3D"6243">[H, W]</code> at end</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6252" data-end=3D"6286">If VRAM becomes tight on your GPU:=
</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6288" data-end=3D"6404">
<li data-start=3D"6288" data-end=3D"6315">
<p data-start=3D"6290" data-end=3D"6315">keep <code data-start=3D"6295" dat=
a-end=3D"6313">base_channels=3D32</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6316" data-end=3D"6342">
<p data-start=3D"6318" data-end=3D"6342">reduce batch size to 1</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6343" data-end=3D"6404">
<p data-start=3D"6345" data-end=3D"6404">(later we can add AMP / mixed prec=
ision to speed things up)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6406" data-end=3D"6409">
<h2 data-start=3D"6411" data-end=3D"6460">4=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Next upgrade =
steps (optional but powerful)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"6462" data-end=3D"6497">Once this UNet is in place, we can=
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6499" data-end=3D"6755">
<li data-start=3D"6499" data-end=3D"6569">
<p data-start=3D"6501" data-end=3D"6569">Add <strong data-start=3D"6505" da=
ta-end=3D"6528">log1p normalization</strong> specifically for <code data-st=
art=3D"6546" data-end=3D"6567">total_precipitation</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6570" data-end=3D"6631">
<p data-start=3D"6572" data-end=3D"6631">Add <strong data-start=3D"6576" da=
ta-end=3D"6601">mixed precision (AMP)</strong> to speed up training on GPU<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6632" data-end=3D"6674">
<p data-start=3D"6634" data-end=3D"6674">Add <strong data-start=3D"6638" da=
ta-end=3D"6672">checkpointing + early stopping</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6675" data-end=3D"6755">
<p data-start=3D"6677" data-end=3D"6755">Optionally build a <strong data-st=
art=3D"6696" data-end=3D"6720">multi-variable model</strong> (several chann=
els in, one var out)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6757" data-end=3D"6785">If you want, next we can do:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6787" data-end=3D"6855">
<li data-start=3D"6787" data-end=3D"6855">
<p data-start=3D"6789" data-end=3D"6855"><strong data-start=3D"6789" data-e=
nd=3D"6795">C)</strong> =E2=80=9COptimize train_model.py for precip (log1p,=
 AMP, LR, etc.)=E2=80=9D</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6857" data-end=3D"6874">For now, you can:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"6876" data-end=3D"7057">
<li data-start=3D"6876" data-end=3D"6904">
<p data-start=3D"6879" data-end=3D"6904">Plug this <code data-start=3D"6889=
" data-end=3D"6899">ZeusUNet</code> in</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6905" data-end=3D"6949">
<p data-start=3D"6908" data-end=3D"6949">Train <code data-start=3D"6914" da=
ta-end=3D"6930">2m_temperature</code> for a few epochs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6950" data-end=3D"7000">
<p data-start=3D"6953" data-end=3D"7000">Train <code data-start=3D"6959" da=
ta-end=3D"6980">total_precipitation</code> for ~20=E2=80=9340 epochs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7001" data-end=3D"7057">
<p data-start=3D"7004" data-end=3D"7057">Share the training loss logs and w=
e can tune further.</p>
</li>
</ol>
