</li>
<li data-start=3D"1879" data-end=3D"1906">
<p data-start=3D"1881" data-end=3D"1906">1024-channel bottleneck</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1907" data-end=3D"1942">
<p data-start=3D"1909" data-end=3D"1942">Precip variable (high variance)</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1943" data-end=3D"1986">
<p data-start=3D"1945" data-end=3D"1986">Input tensor: 24 =C3=97 360 =C3=97=
 720 per sample</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1987" data-end=3D"2023">
<p data-start=3D"1989" data-end=3D"2023">Multi-scale loss doubles compute</=
p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2025" data-end=3D"2060">This naturally takes a ton of VRAM=
.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2062" data-end=3D"2093">Nothing wrong =E2=80=94 this is no=
rmal.</p>
