=3D"12" data-end=3D"38">one variable at a time</strong>, <strong data-start=
=3D"40" data-end=3D"59">NOT all at once</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"62" data-end=3D"91">=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"68" d=
ata-end=3D"91">Sequential Training</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"92" data-end=3D"118">The script runs like this:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"120" data-end=3D"354">
<li data-start=3D"120" data-end=3D"159">
<p data-start=3D"123" data-end=3D"159">Train <code data-start=3D"129" data-=
end=3D"145">2m_temperature</code><br data-start=3D"145" data-end=3D"148">
=E2=86=92 finish</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"160" data-end=3D"208">
<p data-start=3D"163" data-end=3D"208">Train <code data-start=3D"169" data-=
end=3D"194">2m_dewpoint_temperature</code><br data-start=3D"194" data-end=
=3D"197">
=E2=86=92 finish</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"209" data-end=3D"257">
<p data-start=3D"212" data-end=3D"257">Train <code data-start=3D"218" data-=
end=3D"243">10m_u_component_of_wind</code><br data-start=3D"243" data-end=
=3D"246">
=E2=86=92 finish</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"258" data-end=3D"306">
<p data-start=3D"261" data-end=3D"306">Train <code data-start=3D"267" data-=
end=3D"292">10m_v_component_of_wind</code><br>
=E2=86=92 finish</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"307" data-end=3D"323">
<p data-start=3D"310" data-end=3D"323">=E2=80=A6 and so on</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"324" data-end=3D"354">
<p data-start=3D"327" data-end=3D"354">Last: <code data-start=3D"333" data-=
end=3D"354">total_precipitation</code></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"356" data-end=3D"409">So at any moment, <strong data-start=
=3D"374" data-end=3D"408">only 1 training job is running</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"411" data-end=3D"414">
<h1 data-start=3D"416" data-end=3D"439">=E2=9C=85 Why this is correct</h1>
<ul data-start=3D"440" data-end=3D"707">
<li data-start=3D"440" data-end=3D"528">
<p data-start=3D"442" data-end=3D"528">Training 8 UNets <strong data-start=
=3D"459" data-end=3D"477">simultaneously</strong> would cause <strong data-=
start=3D"490" data-end=3D"509">OOM immediately</strong>, even on a 4090.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"529" data-end=3D"707">
<p data-start=3D"531" data-end=3D"559">Sequential training ensures:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"562" data-end=3D"707">
<li data-start=3D"562" data-end=3D"584">
<p data-start=3D"564" data-end=3D"584">GPU not overloaded</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"587" data-end=3D"609">
<p data-start=3D"589" data-end=3D"609">No memory overflow</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"612" data-end=3D"638">
<p data-start=3D"614" data-end=3D"638">Clean log per variable</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"641" data-end=3D"669">
<p data-start=3D"643" data-end=3D"669">Easy resume per variable</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"672" data-end=3D"707">
<p data-start=3D"674" data-end=3D"707">Stable long-running PM2 execution</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
