<p data-start=3D"283" data-end=3D"353">On the <strong data-start=3D"290" da=
ta-end=3D"302">customer</strong> (paid) API, you must include your key, usu=
ally as:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"355" data-end=3D"490">
<li data-start=3D"355" data-end=3D"405">
<p data-start=3D"357" data-end=3D"405">a query parameter: <code data-start=
=3D"376" data-end=3D"394">?apikey=3DYOUR_KEY</code><br data-start=3D"394" d=
ata-end=3D"397">
<strong data-start=3D"399" data-end=3D"405">or</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"406" data-end=3D"490">
<p data-start=3D"408" data-end=3D"490">a header like: <code data-start=3D"4=
23" data-end=3D"457">Authorization: Bearer &lt;YOUR_KEY&gt;</code> (depends=
 on their docs / portal)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"492" data-end=3D"519">They also usually give you:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"521" data-end=3D"636">
<li data-start=3D"521" data-end=3D"592">
<p data-start=3D"523" data-end=3D"592">a <strong data-start=3D"525" data-en=
d=3D"537">base URL</strong> like <code data-start=3D"543" data-end=3D"592">=
https://customer-api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"593" data-end=3D"636">
<ul data-start=3D"595" data-end=3D"636">
<li data-start=3D"595" data-end=3D"636">
<p data-start=3D"597" data-end=3D"636">an <strong data-start=3D"600" data-e=
nd=3D"611">API key</strong> string in the dashboard.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
