<h3 data-start=3D"652" data-end=3D"677">Why they=E2=80=99re different</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"679" data-end=3D"1291">
<li data-start=3D"679" data-end=3D"919">
<p data-start=3D"681" data-end=3D"752"><code data-start=3D"681" data-end=3D=
"689">params</code> =E2=86=92 this is the <strong data-start=3D"704" data-e=
nd=3D"726">original Zeus call</strong> for a <em data-start=3D"733" data-en=
d=3D"750">forecast window</em></p>
<ul data-start=3D"755" data-end=3D"919">
<li data-start=3D"755" data-end=3D"782">
<p data-start=3D"757" data-end=3D"782"><code data-start=3D"757" data-end=3D=
"782">start_hour =3D start_time</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"785" data-end=3D"834">
<p data-start=3D"787" data-end=3D"834"><code data-start=3D"787" data-end=3D=
"808">end_hour =3D end_time</code> (start + requested_hours)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"837" data-end=3D"919">
<p data-start=3D"839" data-end=3D"919">Used when the miner just asks Open-M=
eteo: =E2=80=9CGive me the forecast for the future.=E2=80=9D</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"921" data-end=3D"1291">
<p data-start=3D"923" data-end=3D"1027"><code data-start=3D"923" data-end=
=3D"939">history_params</code> =E2=86=92 this is our <strong data-start=3D"=
954" data-end=3D"969">custom call</strong> to get a <em data-start=3D"979" =
data-end=3D"995">history window</em> for your <strong data-start=3D"1005" d=
ata-end=3D"1025">ML model context</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1030" data-end=3D"1291">
<li data-start=3D"1030" data-end=3D"1168">
<p data-start=3D"1032" data-end=3D"1056">We <em data-start=3D"1035" data-en=
d=3D"1051">want past data</em>, so:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1061" data-end=3D"1168">
<li data-start=3D"1061" data-end=3D"1103">
<p data-start=3D"1063" data-end=3D"1103"><code data-start=3D"1063" data-end=
=3D"1103">history_start =3D start_time - ctx_hours</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1108" data-end=3D"1138">
<p data-start=3D"1110" data-end=3D"1138"><code data-start=3D"1110" data-end=
=3D"1138">start_hour =3D history_start</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1143" data-end=3D"1168">
<p data-start=3D"1145" data-end=3D"1168"><code data-start=3D"1145" data-end=
=3D"1168">end_hour =3D start_time</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1171" data-end=3D"1291">
<p data-start=3D"1173" data-end=3D"1291">That gives you a block like: =E2=
=80=9Cprevious 24/48 hours up to the start time=E2=80=9D<br data-start=3D"1=
245" data-end=3D"1248">
=E2=86=92 exactly what the UNet was trained on.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1293" data-end=3D"1398">So I didn=E2=80=99t =E2=80=9Cchang=
e=E2=80=9D the forecast window logic; I introduced a <strong data-start=3D"=
1356" data-end=3D"1383">separate history window</strong> for the model.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1400" data-end=3D"1413">Conceptually:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1415" data-end=3D"1561">
<li data-start=3D"1415" data-end=3D"1483">
<p data-start=3D"1417" data-end=3D"1483"><code data-start=3D"1417" data-end=
=3D"1425">params</code> =E2=86=92 future: <code data-start=3D"1436" data-en=
d=3D"1460">[start_time, end_time]</code>  =E2=86=92 =E2=80=9Cvalidator hori=
zon=E2=80=9D</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1484" data-end=3D"1561">
<p data-start=3D"1486" data-end=3D"1561"><code data-start=3D"1486" data-end=
=3D"1502">history_params</code> =E2=86=92 past: <code data-start=3D"1511" d=
ata-end=3D"1543">[start_time - ctx, start_time]</code> =E2=86=92 =E2=80=9Cm=
odel context=E2=80=9D</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1563" data-end=3D"1640">Those two windows must be <strong =
data-start=3D"1589" data-end=3D"1602">different</strong> or the model never=
 sees past context.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1642" data-end=3D"1645">
