"402" data-end=3D"408">10=C3=975</code>, <code data-start=3D"410" data-end=
=3D"415">6=C3=976</code>.<br data-start=3D"416" data-end=3D"419">
Your UNet has several <code data-start=3D"441" data-end=3D"477">MaxPool2d(k=
ernel_size=3D2, stride=3D2)</code> downsamples. With small H/W:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"508" data-end=3D"582">
<li data-start=3D"508" data-end=3D"557">
<p data-start=3D"510" data-end=3D"557">5 =E2=86=92 2 =E2=86=92 1 =E2=86=92 =
next pool =E2=86=92 =F0=9F=92=A5 (0 or negative size)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"558" data-end=3D"582">
<p data-start=3D"560" data-end=3D"582">2 =E2=86=92 1 =E2=86=92 next pool =
=E2=86=92 =F0=9F=92=A5</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"584" data-end=3D"604">That=E2=80=99s exactly what:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"606" data-end=3D"658">
<p data-start=3D"608" data-end=3D"658">Given input size (512=C3=971=C3=972)=
 =E2=86=92 output size (512=C3=970=C3=971)</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"660" data-end=3D"666">means.</p>
<p data-start=3D"668" data-end=3D"750">We don=E2=80=99t want to retrain; we=
 just need to make the <strong data-start=3D"719" data-end=3D"737">inferenc=
e side</strong> more robust.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"752" data-end=3D"755">
<h2 data-start=3D"757" data-end=3D"811">=E2=9C=85 Fix: pad small grids befo=
re the model, crop after</h2>
<p data-start=3D"813" data-end=3D"856">We=E2=80=99ll patch <code data-start=
=3D"825" data-end=3D"852">ZeusModelLoader.predict()</code> so:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"858" data-end=3D"1035">
<li data-start=3D"858" data-end=3D"954">
<p data-start=3D"861" data-end=3D"954">If H/W are small, we <strong data-st=
art=3D"882" data-end=3D"889">pad</strong> the tensor to a safe size (like 1=
6=C3=9716 or 32=C3=9732, multiple of 16).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"955" data-end=3D"992">
<p data-start=3D"958" data-end=3D"992">Run the UNet on the padded tensor.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"993" data-end=3D"1035">
<p data-start=3D"996" data-end=3D"1035"><strong data-start=3D"996" data-end=
=3D"1009">Crop back</strong> to the original <code data-start=3D"1026" data=
-end=3D"1034">[H, W]</code>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"1037" data-end=3D"1046">This way:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1048" data-end=3D"1217">
<li data-start=3D"1048" data-end=3D"1088">
<p data-start=3D"1050" data-end=3D"1088">Training stays as-is (global 360=
=C3=97720).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1089" data-end=3D"1141">
<p data-start=3D"1091" data-end=3D"1141">Inference on tiny validator patche=
s doesn=E2=80=99t crash.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1142" data-end=3D"1217">
<p data-start=3D"1144" data-end=3D"1217">The padding just extends edges (re=
plicate), which is fine for a conv net.</p>
</li>
</ul>
