<p data-start=3D"3815" data-end=3D"3836">Key things this does:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3838" data-end=3D"4068">
<li data-start=3D"3838" data-end=3D"3898">
<p data-start=3D"3840" data-end=3D"3898">Works for <strong data-start=3D"38=
50" data-end=3D"3857">any</strong> grid size, including 1=C3=971, 2=C3=972,=
 5=C3=975, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3899" data-end=3D"3981">
<p data-start=3D"3901" data-end=3D"3981">Ensures spatial dims are big/multi=
ple-of-16 so all <code data-start=3D"3952" data-end=3D"3963">MaxPool2d</cod=
e> layers are happy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3982" data-end=3D"4068">
<p data-start=3D"3984" data-end=3D"4068">Keeps your <code data-start=3D"399=
5" data-end=3D"4002">log1p</code> normalization for <code data-start=3D"402=
1" data-end=3D"4042">total_precipitation</code> consistent with training.</=
p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4070" data-end=3D"4134">You do <strong data-start=3D"4077"=
 data-end=3D"4084">not</strong> need to touch <code data-start=3D"4099" dat=
a-end=3D"4109">miner.py</code> for this specific error.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4136" data-end=3D"4139">
<h2 data-start=3D"4141" data-end=3D"4180">2=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Why this fixe=
s your three errors</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4182" data-end=3D"4192">Your logs:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"4194" data-end=3D"4362">
<li data-start=3D"4194" data-end=3D"4252">
<p data-start=3D"4197" data-end=3D"4252"><code data-start=3D"4197" data-end=
=3D"4252">Given input size: (512x1x2) ... output size (512x0x1)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4253" data-end=3D"4303">
<p data-start=3D"4256" data-end=3D"4303"><code data-start=3D"4256" data-end=
=3D"4303">The size of tensor a (3) must match ... b (2)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4304" data-end=3D"4362">
<p data-start=3D"4307" data-end=3D"4362"><code data-start=3D"4307" data-end=
=3D"4362">Given input size: (512x1x1) ... output size (512x0x0)</code></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"4364" data-end=3D"4412">All are classic deep-UNet-on-tiny-=
grid problems:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4414" data-end=3D"4594">
<li data-start=3D"4414" data-end=3D"4479">
<p data-start=3D"4416" data-end=3D"4479">After multiple <code data-start=3D=
"4431" data-end=3D"4440">pool(2)</code> ops, you hit 0 or 1 spatial dimensi=
on.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4480" data-end=3D"4545">
<p data-start=3D"4482" data-end=3D"4545">Up/down blocks can=E2=80=99t line =
up skip connections (<code data-start=3D"4529" data-end=3D"4537">3 vs 2</co=
de> error).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4546" data-end=3D"4594">
<p data-start=3D"4548" data-end=3D"4594">Conv/transpose conv can=E2=80=99t =
handle 0-sized dims.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4596" data-end=3D"4735">Padding to a safe, rounded-up size=
 avoids all of that. The model =E2=80=9Cthinks=E2=80=9D on a 16=C3=9716/32=
=C3=9732 patch, then we trim back to the requested <code data-start=3D"4729=
" data-end=3D"4734">H=C3=97W</code>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4737" data-end=3D"4740">
<h2 data-start=3D"4742" data-end=3D"4783">3=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 You don=E2=80=
=99t need to retrain anything</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4785" data-end=3D"4829">This is purely an <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"4803" data-end=3D"4828">inference wrapper fix</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4831" data-end=3D"4982">
<li data-start=3D"4831" data-end=3D"4875">
<p data-start=3D"4833" data-end=3D"4875">Your <code data-start=3D"4838" dat=
a-end=3D"4843">.pt</code> models remain exactly the same.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4876" data-end=3D"4933">
<p data-start=3D"4878" data-end=3D"4933">Training code (<code data-start=3D=
"4893" data-end=3D"4914">train_model_unet.py</code>) remains the same.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4934" data-end=3D"4982">
<p data-start=3D"4936" data-end=3D"4982">Only <code data-start=3D"4941" dat=
a-end=3D"4968">ZeusModelLoader.predict()</code> gets smarter.</p>
</li>
</ul>
