<p data-start=3D"853" data-end=3D"1087">That=E2=80=99s almost certainly com=
ing from <strong data-start=3D"889" data-end=3D"908">inside the UNet</stron=
g> when the validator sends odd-shaped grids (<code data-start=3D"952" data=
-end=3D"958">6=C3=9715</code>, <code data-start=3D"960" data-end=3D"967">14=
=C3=9715</code>, etc). Even with padding, some weird combo of down/upsampli=
ng and skip connections can still produce off-by-one issues.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1089" data-end=3D"1158">Instead of fighting every internal=
 edge case, we=E2=80=99ll make <code data-start=3D"1146" data-end=3D"1157">=
predict()</code>:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"1160" data-end=3D"1446">
<li data-start=3D"1160" data-end=3D"1215">
<p data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1215"><strong data-start=3D"1163" data-e=
nd=3D"1176">Normalize</strong> input (z-score or <code data-start=3D"1195" =
data-end=3D"1202">log1p</code> for precip).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1216" data-end=3D"1259">
<p data-start=3D"1219" data-end=3D"1259"><strong data-start=3D"1219" data-e=
nd=3D"1226">Pad</strong> to a safe size (multiple of 16).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1260" data-end=3D"1284">
<p data-start=3D"1263" data-end=3D"1284">Try to run the model.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1285" data-end=3D"1446">
<p data-start=3D"1288" data-end=3D"1446">If the model crashes with a <code =
data-start=3D"1316" data-end=3D"1330">RuntimeError</code>, we <strong data-=
start=3D"1335" data-end=3D"1366">fallback to a safe baseline</strong>: repe=
at the last context frame for all forecast steps (so miner never crashes).<=
/p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"1448" data-end=3D"1457">This way:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1459" data-end=3D"1589">
<li data-start=3D"1459" data-end=3D"1510">
<p data-start=3D"1461" data-end=3D"1510">Big normal grids use your heavy tr=
ained model =E2=9C=85</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1511" data-end=3D"1589">
<p data-start=3D"1513" data-end=3D"1589">Tiny / weird grids won=E2=80=99t c=
rash, they just fall back to =E2=80=9Cconstant=E2=80=9D forecast =E2=9C=85<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
