<p data-start=3D"4774" data-end=3D"4807">This does three important things:<=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"4809" data-end=3D"5066">
<li data-start=3D"4809" data-end=3D"4856">
<p data-start=3D"4811" data-end=3D"4856">Uses <code data-start=3D"4816" dat=
a-end=3D"4823">F.pad</code> safely (with the import at top).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4857" data-end=3D"4925">
<p data-start=3D"4859" data-end=3D"4925">Avoids UNet =E2=80=9Coutput size i=
s too small=E2=80=9D for tiny grids via padding.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4926" data-end=3D"5066">
<p data-start=3D"4928" data-end=3D"5066">If UNet <em data-start=3D"4936" da=
ta-end=3D"4943">still</em> explodes for some weird shape / architecture mis=
match, we catch the exception and fallback instead of crashing your miner.<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
