<p data-start=3D"5828" data-end=3D"5862">You should keep seeing lines like:=
</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5864" data-end=3D"6109">
<li data-start=3D"5864" data-end=3D"5905">
<p data-start=3D"5866" data-end=3D"5905"><code data-start=3D"5866" data-end=
=3D"5905">Output shape =E2=86=92 torch.Size([3, 5, 11])</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5906" data-end=3D"5947">
<p data-start=3D"5908" data-end=3D"5947"><code data-start=3D"5908" data-end=
=3D"5947">Output shape =E2=86=92 torch.Size([15, 9, 5])</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5948" data-end=3D"6109">
<p data-start=3D"5950" data-end=3D"6109">And <em data-start=3D"5954" data-e=
nd=3D"5971">maybe sometimes</em>: <code data-start=3D"5973" data-end=3D"605=
2">[ModelLoader] WARNING: model forward failed for 100m_u_component_of_wind=
: ...</code><br data-start=3D"6052" data-end=3D"6055">
but <strong data-start=3D"6061" data-end=3D"6090">no more hard RuntimeError=
</strong> in the miner logs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6111" data-end=3D"6262">If you still see a crash after thi=
s (with a new stack or message), paste that new error and we=E2=80=99ll squ=
ash that one too. But from here, you=E2=80=99re basically:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6264" data-end=3D"6439">
<li data-start=3D"6264" data-end=3D"6288">
<p data-start=3D"6266" data-end=3D"6288">answering all queries,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6289" data-end=3D"6321">
<p data-start=3D"6291" data-end=3D"6321">stable under weird tiny grids,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6322" data-end=3D"6367">
<p data-start=3D"6324" data-end=3D"6367">using your trained models most of =
the time,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6368" data-end=3D"6439">
<p data-start=3D"6370" data-end=3D"6439">and only falling back to =E2=80=9C=
persistence=E2=80=9D when the fancy UNet complains.</p>
</li>
</ul>
