an>:
                </span><span><span class=3D"hljs-comment"># worst-case =E2=
=80=93 make something valid</span></span><span>
                last =3D torch.zeros(H, W)

            pred =3D last.unsqueeze(</span><span><span class=3D"hljs-number=
">0</span></span><span>).repeat(F_hours, </span><span><span class=3D"hljs-n=
umber">1</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class=3D"hljs-number">1</s=
pan></span><span>).cpu().numpy()
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start=3D"2359" data-end=3D"2441">So even if <code data-start=3D"237=
0" data-end=3D"2384">model_loader</code> ever throws, the miner always retu=
rns a valid <code data-start=3D"2431" data-end=3D"2440">[T,H,W]</code>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2443" data-end=3D"2545">You already did most of this, but =
double-check that <code data-start=3D"2495" data-end=3D"2510">Miner.forward=
</code> actually wraps the call like this.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2547" data-end=3D"2550">
<h2 data-start=3D"2552" data-end=3D"2602">2=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Are the u100 =
/ v100 <em data-start=3D"2579" data-end=3D"2594">badly trained</em>? Maybe.=
</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2604" data-end=3D"2638">Totally fair suspicion. Winds are:=
</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2640" data-end=3D"2743">
<li data-start=3D"2640" data-end=3D"2654">
<p data-start=3D"2642" data-end=3D"2654">More noisy</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2655" data-end=3D"2695">
<p data-start=3D"2657" data-end=3D"2695">More symmetric (positive &amp; neg=
ative)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2696" data-end=3D"2743">
<p data-start=3D"2698" data-end=3D"2743">More sensitive to resolution and t=
ime context</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2745" data-end=3D"2769">It=E2=80=99s very possible that:</=
p>
<ul data-start=3D"2771" data-end=3D"2981">
<li data-start=3D"2771" data-end=3D"2860">
<p data-start=3D"2773" data-end=3D"2860"><code data-start=3D"2773" data-end=
=3D"2779">u100</code> / <code data-start=3D"2782" data-end=3D"2788">v100</c=
ode> were trained with <strong data-start=3D"2807" data-end=3D"2834">earlie=
r, smaller models</strong> (e.g., CPU simple UNet)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2861" data-end=3D"2917">
<p data-start=3D"2863" data-end=3D"2917">Or with <strong data-start=3D"2871=
" data-end=3D"2887">fewer epochs</strong> / less data than the others</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2918" data-end=3D"2981">
<p data-start=3D"2920" data-end=3D"2981">Or that they suffer from <strong d=
ata-start=3D"2945" data-end=3D"2981">slightly different normalization</stro=
ng></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2983" data-end=3D"3013">Easy sanity checks you can do:</p>
