<p data-start=3D"3920" data-end=3D"3986">Your <code data-start=3D"3925" dat=
a-end=3D"3942">ZeusModelLoader</code> will pick up the new weights automati=
cally.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3988" data-end=3D"3991">
<h2 data-start=3D"3993" data-end=3D"4030">4=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 What happens =
after retraining?</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"4032" data-end=3D"4542">
<li data-start=3D"4032" data-end=3D"4321">
<p data-start=3D"4034" data-end=3D"4048">For u100/v100:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4051" data-end=3D"4321">
<li data-start=3D"4051" data-end=3D"4186">
<p data-start=3D"4053" data-end=3D"4186">The UNet is still big, so some wei=
rd tiny grids may still hit architecture limits =E2=86=92 those calls will =
hit your fallback (that=E2=80=99s okay).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4189" data-end=3D"4321">
<p data-start=3D"4191" data-end=3D"4231">But on =E2=80=9Cnormal=E2=80=9D gr=
ids, the model should:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4236" data-end=3D"4321">
<li data-start=3D"4236" data-end=3D"4265">
<p data-start=3D"4238" data-end=3D"4265">Run successfully more often</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4270" data-end=3D"4321">
<p data-start=3D"4272" data-end=3D"4321">Be more accurate (lower loss =E2=
=86=92 better Zeus score)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4323" data-end=3D"4542">
<p data-start=3D"4325" data-end=3D"4340">For the subnet:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4343" data-end=3D"4542">
<li data-start=3D"4343" data-end=3D"4399">
<p data-start=3D"4345" data-end=3D"4399">Validators will see <strong data-s=
tart=3D"4365" data-end=3D"4399">valid predictions all the time</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4402" data-end=3D"4456">
<p data-start=3D"4404" data-end=3D"4456">For most requests, they=E2=80=99ll=
 use your <strong data-start=3D"4440" data-end=3D"4454">real model</strong>=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4459" data-end=3D"4542">
<p data-start=3D"4461" data-end=3D"4542">Only for pathological edge-case gr=
ids, they=E2=80=99ll get fallback (repeated last hour).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4544" data-end=3D"4591">That=E2=80=99s totally acceptable =
behavior for a miner.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4593" data-end=3D"4596">
<p data-start=3D"4598" data-end=3D"4648">If you want, next step after retra=
ining those two:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4650" data-end=3D"4848">
<li data-start=3D"4650" data-end=3D"4848">
<p data-start=3D"4652" data-end=3D"4711">We can wire up a small <code data-=
start=3D"4675" data-end=3D"4699">offline_eval_u_v100.py</code> to compare:<=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"4714" data-end=3D"4848">
<li data-start=3D"4714" data-end=3D"4760">
<p data-start=3D"4716" data-end=3D"4760">your model vs Open-Meteo on a samp=
le period,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4763" data-end=3D"4790">
<p data-start=3D"4765" data-end=3D"4790">error metrics (MAE/RMSE),</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4793" data-end=3D"4848">
<p data-start=3D"4795" data-end=3D"4848">and see if u100/v100 are still lag=
ging behind others.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4850" data-end=3D"4863">But in short:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4865" data-end=3D"5063">
<li data-start=3D"4865" data-end=3D"4924">
<p data-start=3D"4867" data-end=3D"4924">Yes, retraining <strong data-start=
=3D"4883" data-end=3D"4908">just these two models</strong> is a good idea.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4925" data-end=3D"5063">
<p data-start=3D"4927" data-end=3D"5063">Your miner is already robust; retr=
aining will mainly <strong data-start=3D"4980" data-end=3D"4999">improve qu=
ality</strong>, not <strong data-start=3D"5005" data-end=3D"5020">fix crash=
es</strong> (crashes are already handled by fallback).</p>
</li>
</ul>
