<p data-start=3D"347" data-end=3D"521">Grid is <code data-start=3D"355" dat=
a-end=3D"367">[H=3D8, W=3D5]</code> =E2=80=93 once you downsample multiple =
times in the deep UNet (MaxPool2d), one side becomes too small (1, 0=E2=80=
=A6), and ConvTranspose2d + skips start fighting =E2=86=92 boom.</p>
<p data-start=3D"523" data-end=3D"686">Even if we added a <code data-start=
=3D"542" data-end=3D"554">try/except</code> in <code data-start=3D"558" dat=
a-end=3D"573">Miner.forward</code>, if the error happens in a part not wrap=
ped correctly or in a different version of the code, you still see this.</p=
>
<p data-start=3D"688" data-end=3D"750">So let=E2=80=99s make this <strong d=
ata-start=3D"707" data-end=3D"749">bullet-proof at the model loader level</=
strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"752" data-end=3D"989">
<li data-start=3D"752" data-end=3D"824">
<p data-start=3D"754" data-end=3D"824">For <strong data-start=3D"758" data-=
end=3D"773">small grids</strong> (like 8=C3=975, 6=C3=974, etc.), we <stron=
g data-start=3D"800" data-end=3D"809">never</strong> call the UNet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"825" data-end=3D"907">
<p data-start=3D"827" data-end=3D"907">Instead, we immediately use <strong =
data-start=3D"855" data-end=3D"879">persistence fallback</strong> (repeat l=
ast context step).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"908" data-end=3D"989">
<p data-start=3D"910" data-end=3D"931">For normal grids, we:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"935" data-end=3D"989">
<li data-start=3D"935" data-end=3D"947">
<p data-start=3D"937" data-end=3D"947">Try UNet</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"950" data-end=3D"989">
<p data-start=3D"952" data-end=3D"989">On <em data-start=3D"955" data-end=
=3D"960">any</em> exception, log and fallback.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"991" data-end=3D"1089">This way, even if miner=E2=80=99s <=
code data-start=3D"1017" data-end=3D"1026">forward</code> isn=E2=80=99t wra=
pped perfectly, the loader itself will <em data-start=3D"1075" data-end=3D"=
1082">never</em> throw.</p>
