<p data-start=3D"1461" data-end=3D"1566">already mean <strong data-start=3D=
"1474" data-end=3D"1514">the saved <code data-start=3D"1486" data-end=3D"14=
91">.pt</code> file can=E2=80=99t be reused</strong> =E2=80=93 PyTorch will=
 say =E2=80=9Csize mismatch=E2=80=9D for many layers.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1568" data-end=3D"1571">So:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1573" data-end=3D"1721">
<li data-start=3D"1573" data-end=3D"1625">
<p data-start=3D"1575" data-end=3D"1625">Architecturally: <strong data-star=
t=3D"1592" data-end=3D"1623">they are cousins, not twins</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1626" data-end=3D"1721">
<p data-start=3D"1628" data-end=3D"1721">Practically: <strong data-start=3D=
"1641" data-end=3D"1661">you MUST retrain</strong> if you switch from ZeusU=
Net =E2=86=92 WindUNet for 100m_u / 100m_v.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1723" data-end=3D"1726">
<h3 data-start=3D"1728" data-end=3D"1758">3. What this means for you</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1760" data-end=3D"2313">
<li data-start=3D"1760" data-end=3D"1872">
<p data-start=3D"1762" data-end=3D"1872">For <strong data-start=3D"1766" da=
ta-end=3D"1805">2m temp, dewpoint, pressure, precip</strong>:<br data-start=
=3D"1806" data-end=3D"1809">
Your current ZeusUNet models are fine. No need to touch them.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1874" data-end=3D"2313">
<p data-start=3D"1876" data-end=3D"1902">For <strong data-start=3D"1880" da=
ta-end=3D"1899">100m_u / 100m_v</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1905" data-end=3D"2313">
<li data-start=3D"1905" data-end=3D"2007">
<p data-start=3D"1907" data-end=3D"2007">Right now: ZeusUNet + our safety w=
rapper + persistence fallback =E2=86=92 works, but sometimes shape issues.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2010" data-end=3D"2313">
<p data-start=3D"2012" data-end=3D"2055">If you adopt <strong data-start=3D=
"2025" data-end=3D"2037">WindUNet</strong>, do it like this:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"2060" data-end=3D"2313">
<li data-start=3D"2060" data-end=3D"2141">
<p data-start=3D"2063" data-end=3D"2141">Change <code data-start=3D"2070" d=
ata-end=3D"2091">train_model_unet.py</code> to use <code data-start=3D"2099=
" data-end=3D"2109">WindUNet</code> <em data-start=3D"2110" data-end=3D"211=
6">only</em> for those two variables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2146" data-end=3D"2238">
<p data-start=3D"2149" data-end=3D"2166">Retrain <strong data-start=3D"2157=
" data-end=3D"2165">only</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2174" data-end=3D"2238">
<li data-start=3D"2174" data-end=3D"2202">
<p data-start=3D"2176" data-end=3D"2202"><code data-start=3D"2176" data-end=
=3D"2202">100m_u_component_of_wind</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2210" data-end=3D"2238">
<p data-start=3D"2212" data-end=3D"2238"><code data-start=3D"2212" data-end=
=3D"2238">100m_v_component_of_wind</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2243" data-end=3D"2313">
<p data-start=3D"2246" data-end=3D"2313">Keep the old ZeusUNet checkpoints =
as backup (rename to <code data-start=3D"2301" data-end=3D"2311">*_old.pt</=
code>).</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2315" data-end=3D"2397">After retraining, model_loader + m=
iner can safely use WindUNet and you should see:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2399" data-end=3D"2548">
<li data-start=3D"2399" data-end=3D"2449">
<p data-start=3D"2401" data-end=3D"2449">no more conv-transpose size mismat=
ch on winds,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2450" data-end=3D"2492">
<p data-start=3D"2452" data-end=3D"2492">better behaviour on weird grid sha=
pes,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2493" data-end=3D"2548">
<p data-start=3D"2495" data-end=3D"2548">potentially better score on Zeus f=
or those variables.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2550" data-end=3D"2579">If you want, next step I can:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2581" data-end=3D"2728">
<li data-start=3D"2581" data-end=3D"2728">
<p data-start=3D"2583" data-end=3D"2611">give you a <strong data-start=3D"2=
594" data-end=3D"2608">clean diff</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2614" data-end=3D"2728">
<li data-start=3D"2614" data-end=3D"2684">
<p data-start=3D"2616" data-end=3D"2684">how to plug <code data-start=3D"26=
28" data-end=3D"2638">WindUNet</code> into <code data-start=3D"2644" data-e=
nd=3D"2665">train_model_unet.py</code> <em data-start=3D"2666" data-end=3D"=
2682">only for winds</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2687" data-end=3D"2728">
<p data-start=3D"2689" data-end=3D"2728">and keep everything else exactly a=
s is.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
