<p data-start=3D"106" data-end=3D"117">That error:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"119" data-end=3D"212">
<p data-start=3D"121" data-end=3D"212"><code data-start=3D"121" data-end=3D=
"212">The size of tensor a (4) must match the size of tensor b (3) at non-s=
ingleton dimension 2</code></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"214" data-end=3D"453">is coming from the <strong data-star=
t=3D"233" data-end=3D"258">UNet down/up-sampling</strong> when the grid is =
small (like 7=C3=977, 8=C3=975, 15=C3=9711, etc).<br data-start=3D"310" dat=
a-end=3D"313">
Each <code data-start=3D"318" data-end=3D"332">MaxPool2d(2)</code> halves t=
he size; after several levels you get weird odd sizes (3, 4, 5=E2=80=A6) an=
d the up path can=E2=80=99t line up perfectly =E2=86=92 boom.</p>
<p data-start=3D"455" data-end=3D"525">Retraining 100m_u / 100m_v <strong d=
ata-start=3D"482" data-end=3D"503">does not fix this</strong>.<br data-star=
t=3D"504" data-end=3D"507">
You=E2=80=99d need either:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"718">
<li data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"606">
<p data-start=3D"529" data-end=3D"606">a <strong data-start=3D"531" data-en=
d=3D"557">shallower architecture</strong> (WindUNet with fewer pools), <em =
data-start=3D"587" data-end=3D"592">and</em> retrain, or</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"607" data-end=3D"718">
<p data-start=3D"609" data-end=3D"718">a <strong data-start=3D"611" data-en=
d=3D"628">runtime guard</strong>: for grids that are =E2=80=9Ctoo small=E2=
=80=9D, don=E2=80=99t use the CNN at all, just fall back to persistence.</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"720" data-end=3D"772">Right now the fastest safe fix is th=
e second option.</p>
