<p data-start=3D"4201" data-end=3D"4287">For <strong data-start=3D"4205" da=
ta-end=3D"4218">big grids</strong> (e.g. 32=C3=9732, 40=C3=9740):<br data-s=
tart=3D"4239" data-end=3D"4242">
=E2=86=92 100m wind models still run with the UNet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4289" data-end=3D"4575">
<p data-start=3D"4291" data-end=3D"4508">For <strong data-start=3D"4295" da=
ta-end=3D"4318">small / weird grids</strong> (like 16=C3=977, 8=C3=9711, 5=
=C3=977 etc, where you=E2=80=99re seeing<br data-start=3D"4365" data-end=3D=
"4368">
<code data-start=3D"4370" data-end=3D"4432">The size of tensor a (4) must m=
atch the size of tensor b (3)</code>):<br data-start=3D"4434" data-end=3D"4=
437">
=E2=86=92 we never even call the CNN.<br data-start=3D"4468" data-end=3D"44=
71">
Miner just returns persistence, so:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4511" data-end=3D"4575">
<li data-start=3D"4511" data-end=3D"4531">
<p data-start=3D"4513" data-end=3D"4531">no <code data-start=3D"4516" data-=
end=3D"4530">RuntimeError</code>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4534" data-end=3D"4575">
<p data-start=3D"4536" data-end=3D"4575">validator still gets valid predict=
ions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4577" data-end=3D"4602">Later, when you=E2=80=99re ready:<=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"4604" data-end=3D"4858">
<li data-start=3D"4604" data-end=3D"4693">
<p data-start=3D"4606" data-end=3D"4693">define <strong data-start=3D"4613"=
 data-end=3D"4625">WindUNet</strong> with fewer downsampling levels (e.g. 2=
=E2=80=933 maxpools instead of 4+),</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4694" data-end=3D"4769">
<p data-start=3D"4696" data-end=3D"4769">retrain only <code data-start=3D"4=
709" data-end=3D"4735">100m_u_component_of_wind</code> and <code data-start=
=3D"4740" data-end=3D"4766">100m_v_component_of_wind</code>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4770" data-end=3D"4858">
<p data-start=3D"4772" data-end=3D"4858">and then you can relax the cutoff =
in <code data-start=3D"4809" data-end=3D"4828">_use_cnn_for_wind</code> (ma=
ybe down to min(H,W) =E2=89=A5 8).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4860" data-end=3D"5022">For now, adding this small-grid gu=
ard + try/except <strong data-start=3D"4911" data-end=3D"4942">will stop th=
ose wind errors</strong> without touching your already-good models for temp=
, dewpoint, pressure, precip.</p>
